  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "The Context-Switch Problem",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three States, One Repo",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Working tree = files on disk you edit",
            "Index = what `git add` recorded, staged",
            "HEAD = the commit currently checked out",
            "Stash and worktrees both move these three"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Refusal That Starts It"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ git switch release-2.x",
            "error: Your local changes to the",
            "following files would be overwritten",
            "by checkout:  src/parser.js",
            "Please commit or stash them."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A dirty switch works if the file is identical",
            "in both commits — Git carries the edit across",
            "Only conflicting paths fail",
            "That is why the error feels random"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Four Escape Hatches"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Hatch",
            "Speed",
            "Isolation"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Commit WIP",
              "fast",
              "none"
            ],
            [
              "Stash",
              "fast",
              "none"
            ],
            [
              "Worktree",
              "medium",
              "high"
            ],
            [
              "Second clone",
              "slow",
              "total"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A WIP commit pollutes history",
            "Forces `--amend` or rebase cleanup later",
            "Stash keeps history clean",
            "But hides the work off-branch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Shapes Of Answer"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stash: stack of temp commits, one checkout",
            "Worktree: many checkouts, one object database",
            "Stash time-multiplexes; worktree space-multiplexes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Minutes vs days",
          "text": "Stash for interruptions measured in minutes. Worktree for parallel work measured in hours or days."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Classic blind spot",
          "items": [
            "Untracked and ignored files",
            "Branch switch ignores them",
            "Plain `git stash` ignores them too",
            "They survive the switch and collide"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Your First Stash"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash              # alias of push",
            "git stash push -m \"wip: parser fix\"",
            "git stash list  # stash@{0} is newest"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Push rolls tracked + staged back to HEAD",
            "Unlabeled entries read 'WIP on main: 3f2a1 ...'",
            "Three of those and the labels stop meaning anything",
            "Indices renumber whenever an entry is dropped"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git fsck --unreachable | grep commit",
            "git show <sha>        # identify it",
            "git stash apply <sha>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Restoring Stashes & Stash Anatomy",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git worktree add -b hotfix-501 \\",
            "  ../hotfix origin/main",
            "# fix, test, push",
            "git worktree remove ../hotfix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Look Before You Restore",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash show stash@{1}    # diffstat",
            "git stash show -p stash@{1} # full patch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Restore, Keep Or Kill"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Restores",
            "Entry after"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "apply",
              "yes",
              "kept"
            ],
            [
              "pop",
              "yes",
              "dropped"
            ],
            [
              "drop",
              "no",
              "gone"
            ],
            [
              "clear",
              "no",
              "all gone"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`git stash drop stash@{2}` kills one entry",
            "`git stash clear` asks nothing",
            "And undoes nothing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Clean Rescue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash branch salvage stash@{0}",
            "# branch at the stash's parent commit",
            "# applies there, drops it on success"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Facts People Miss"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Staged changes come back unstaged without `--index`",
            "Stash is per-repository, never per-branch",
            "A stash from `feature-a` pops fine on `main`",
            "Git will not warn you about that"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "A Stash Entry Is A Commit"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "stash commit: tree = working tree",
              "parent 1 = HEAD at stash time",
              "parent 2 = index / staged state",
              "parent 3 = untracked, only with -u"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Normally 2 parents, 3 when `-u`/`-a` used",
            "Parent 2's tree holds the index state",
            "That split is why `--index` restores exactly"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where The Stack Lives"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git log --graph --oneline refs/stash",
            "git cat-file -p refs/stash  # parent list"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`refs/stash` is one ref; the stack is its reflog",
            "`stash@{1}` = reflog entry 1 of `refs/stash`",
            "Drop `stash@{0}` and old `{1}` becomes `{0}`",
            "Scripts hardcoding indices break"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Dropped Is Not Deleted",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stash commits are unreachable from any branch",
            "So they are garbage-collection candidates",
            "Window = `gc.reflogExpireUnreachable`, 30 days"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Recovery, apply vs pop",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Recover A Dropped Stash"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git fsck --unreachable | grep commit",
            "git stash apply <sha>",
            "git branch rescue <sha>   # safer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Scriptable Primitives"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash create   # prints a SHA only",
            "# stack and working tree untouched",
            "git stash store -m msg <sha>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "pop = apply + drop"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`pop` drops only if the apply was clean",
            "Conflicted pop: partial apply AND entry kept",
            "Resolving the conflict does not auto-drop it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Duplicate trap",
          "text": "Read `git stash list` right after a conflicted pop, or you reapply the same change days later."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Side By Side"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "apply",
            "pop"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Safety",
              "keeps backup",
              "deletes it"
            ],
            [
              "Hygiene",
              "stack rots",
              "stays clean"
            ],
            [
              "Conflict",
              "recoverable",
              "recoverable"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Prefer `apply` when the target moved far from base",
            "`apply` replays one WIP onto two branches",
            "e.g. test a fix on `main` and `release/2.x`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Replay One WIP Twice"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash apply stash@{0}   # on main",
            "npm test",
            "git checkout -- .   # reset the tree",
            "git switch release/2.x",
            "git stash apply stash@{0}   # again"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "--index And The 3-Way"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--index` restores the staged/unstaged split",
            "It fails outright if the index cannot be rebuilt",
            "Plain apply degrades to everything unstaged",
            "Applying is a merge, not a patch application",
            "3-way survives moved files and changed context"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Default Move"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash apply   # restore",
            "npm test          # verify it builds",
            "git stash drop    # then clean up"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`-u` stores untracked as the third parent",
            "Without it, new files stay and collide on switch",
            "`-a` near `node_modules/` stashes gigabytes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`-k` leaves the staged version on disk",
            "You test exactly what you are about to commit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Surgical Stashing"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash push -p     # pick hunks",
            "git stash push -m msg -- src/lexer.js"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Stash Flags & Your First Worktree",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Gets Swept Up",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Tracked",
            "Untracked",
            "Ignored"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "(none)",
              "yes",
              "no",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "-u",
              "yes",
              "yes",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "-a",
              "yes",
              "yes",
              "yes"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Keep-Index Pre-Commit Test"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git add src/parser.js",
            "git stash push -k -m \"unstaged rest\"",
            "npm test     # runs only the staged code",
            "git stash pop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "--staged, The Inverse"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Git 2.35+: stashes only staged changes",
            "Unstaged work stays in the tree untouched",
            "Exactly the mirror of `--keep-index`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`-p` splits one messy edit: park half, keep half",
            "Pathspec form stashes only those paths",
            "`-u` combined with a pathspec works fine"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two flag traps",
          "items": [
            "No changes: 'No local changes to save'",
            "Nothing pushed — check exit status in scripts",
            "`-k` with `-p` surprises people",
            "The kept index is the pre-stash one"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Your First Worktree"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git worktree add ../hotfix hotfix-br",
            "git worktree add -b fix-123 ../fix-123",
            "git worktree add --detach ../scratch HEAD"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Second directory, same `.git` object database",
            "Original is the main worktree, rest are linked",
            "`git worktree list`: path, HEAD sha, branch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What The Trees Share",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Objects, refs, config, remotes and hooks",
            "One `git fetch` updates every worktree",
            "No re-clone, no second fetch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Disk cost is one checkout of files",
            "Not a second copy of history",
            "Huge saving over a clone on a fat `.git`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Administration"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git worktree remove ../hotfix",
            "git worktree prune   # after a manual rm",
            "git worktree move ../old ../new"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`move` fixes internal path pointers — never `mv`",
            "`lock` stops prune reaping unmounted storage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git worktree lock ../on-usb \\",
            "  --reason \"removable drive\""
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--force` overrides the hard rule",
            "Then two indexes race on one ref",
            "Only do it if you understand that"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Worktree Internals & Ref Scope",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Shared stack",
          "text": "Each worktree has its own HEAD and index, but `refs/stash` is shared across all of them. That surprises everyone once."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The .git File"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ cat ../hotfix/.git",
            "gitdir: /repo/.git/worktrees/hotfix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A linked worktree has a `.git` file, not a directory",
            "`.git/worktrees/<name>/`: HEAD, index, reflogs",
            "Plus `commondir` and `gitdir`",
            "`commondir` points back at the shared `.git`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Per-Worktree vs Shared"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Ref",
            "Scope"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "HEAD",
              "per-worktree"
            ],
            [
              "refs/bisect/*",
              "per-worktree"
            ],
            [
              "refs/worktree/*",
              "per-worktree"
            ],
            [
              "branches, tags",
              "shared"
            ],
            [
              "refs/stash",
              "shared"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "One Branch, One Tree"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ git worktree add ../x main",
            "fatal: 'main' is already checked out",
            "at '/repo'"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The #1 Worktree Error",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Adding a worktree on an already-checked-out branch",
            "Fix: `--detach`, or a new branch off it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git worktree add --detach ../scratch main",
            "git worktree add -b review-main ../r main"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Scripts That Assume One .git"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git rev-parse --git-dir   # this worktree",
            "git rev-parse --git-common-dir  # shared"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$GIT_DIR` differs per worktree",
            "Hardcoded `.git/` paths break in linked trees"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Per-Worktree Config"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git config extensions.worktreeConfig true",
            "git config --worktree core.hooksPath .hooks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two more rules",
          "items": [
            "Submodules in linked worktrees are fragile",
            "Verify before relying on them",
            "`rm -rf` leaves a stale `worktree list` entry",
            "It stays until you `prune`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Which Tool Wins"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Tool"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Clean tree, quick hop",
              "git switch"
            ],
            [
              "30s interrupt, small diff",
              "stash"
            ],
            [
              "Long parallel work",
              "worktree"
            ],
            [
              "Hot build state",
              "worktree"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Branch switch: zero admin overhead",
            "Stash: same artifacts, no processes to restart",
            "Worktree: dev server stays up, both versions visible"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Killer Cases & Real Costs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where Worktrees Are Unbeatable"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Side by side: diff behavior, run both test suites",
            "Open both versions in the editor at once",
            "Stash simply cannot do this"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "10-minute build: switching kills `node_modules`",
            "Also `target/`, `__pycache__`, compiler caches",
            "A second worktree keeps each build hot",
            "Long review: PR in `../review`, feature untouched"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where Stash Is Unbeatable",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash && git pull --rebase && \\",
            "  git stash pop   # pull blocked by noise"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pre-commit check: `--keep-index`, then run tests",
            "You verify exactly the staged change"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worktree Or Second Clone"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "Worktree",
            "Clone"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Objects",
              "shared",
              "copied"
            ],
            [
              "Fetches",
              "one",
              "two"
            ],
            [
              "Config/hooks",
              "shared",
              "isolated"
            ],
            [
              "Pick when",
              "cheap parallel",
              "tool edits config"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Not storage",
          "text": "Stash as long-term storage is an anti-pattern. Anything you would be sad to lose belongs on a branch."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Time Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Operation",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "stash push/pop",
              "diff size + tree write"
            ],
            [
              "worktree add",
              "checkout I/O only"
            ],
            [
              "full clone",
              "whole object db"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stash is effectively instant on typical diffs",
            "Worktree add copies no objects, just admin bytes",
            "A 2 GB `.git` clone becomes 4 GB on disk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Mental Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An unlabeled stash stack is opaque",
            "Entries carry no branch context at all",
            "Worktrees: many dirs, each indexed by your IDE",
            "Tooling assuming one checkout misbehaves"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "gc roots",
          "text": "`git gc` runs on the shared object store, so it must treat every worktree's HEAD and index as roots. Prune before gc."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two worktrees run `status` and builds at once",
            "One working tree cannot",
            "Some ops still lock shared refs repo-wide"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Storage, Scaling & Common Slips",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Storage Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One commit + trees + blobs per stash entry",
            "Deduplicated against existing objects — cheap",
            "Unless `-a` swallowed your build output",
            "`clone --shared`/`--reference` skips the copy",
            "But leaves a fragile link to the source repo"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How Each Scales",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Count",
            "Stash",
            "Worktrees"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1-2",
              "fine",
              "fine"
            ],
            [
              "~5",
              "degrades",
              "fine"
            ],
            [
              ">5",
              "opaque stack",
              "disk + indexing"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stash Slips And Fixes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Slip",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "pop on a moved base",
              "git stash branch"
            ],
            [
              "No -u, then clean -fd",
              "nothing — gone"
            ],
            [
              "clear to 'tidy up'",
              "fsck, gc window"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The stash base commit differs, so the pop conflicts",
            "`git stash branch <name>` reapplies on that base",
            "Default to `git stash push -u` and stop losing files",
            "`clear` makes entries unreachable immediately"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Duplicate Loop"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Conflicted pop, resolve, commit — entry still there",
            "Later you pop it and reapply the same change",
            "Read `git stash list` right after resolving"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stashes Are Not Branch-Bound"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "It does not belong to the branch you made it on",
            "Read the 'WIP on <branch>' text before popping"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ git stash list",
            "stash@{0}: WIP on feature-a: 3f2a1 lexer",
            "stash@{1}: On main: wip: parser fix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worktree Slips And Fixes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Slip",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "rm -rf the directory",
              "git worktree prune"
            ],
            [
              "add on live branch",
              "--detach or new br"
            ],
            [
              "hardcoded .git path",
              "--git-common-dir"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "HOOKS=$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/hooks",
            "# correct in main and linked worktrees"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Deleting a branch a linked worktree holds is blocked",
            "Force-deleting leaves that worktree on an orphan ref"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "pop Is Not Atomic",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash pop || echo \"conflict!\"",
            "git stash list    # verify it is gone"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Never assume a scripted pop succeeded",
            "Check the exit code, then inspect the list"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Everyday Recipes & Decision Table",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Interruption"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash push -u -m \"wip: checkout flow\"",
            "# fix the bug, commit it",
            "git stash pop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Test Only The Staged Half"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git add -p",
            "git stash push --keep-index -m \"rest\"",
            "npm test && git commit",
            "git stash pop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Wrong Branch, Right Fix"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash -u",
            "git switch -c correct-branch",
            "git stash pop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rescue And Recover"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash branch salvage stash@{0}",
            "# merge or cherry-pick from salvage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worktree Recipes"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git fetch origin pull/123/head:pr-123",
            "git worktree add ../review pr-123",
            "git worktree remove ../review"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Side by side: add `../v1 v1.0` and `../v2 v2.0`",
            "Run both, diff the outputs directly",
            "Bisect: `git worktree add ../bisect --detach`",
            "Bisect refs are per-worktree — workspace safe",
            "Sweep: `list`, `remove` each, `prune`, then `stash list`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Two Models",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stash: hidden 2-or-3-parent commits in `refs/stash`",
            "Indexed by reflog position, one working tree",
            "Worktree: extra directory, own HEAD and index",
            "Shared object store, listed in `.git/worktrees/`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "apply vs pop, Final Word"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`apply` keeps the entry, always",
            "`pop` drops it on a clean apply only",
            "After any conflict, verify `git stash list` yourself"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Decision Table"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Choose"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<10 min, small diff",
              "stash"
            ],
            [
              "Parallel or hot build",
              "worktree"
            ],
            [
              "Side-by-side compare",
              "worktree"
            ],
            [
              "Isolated config/hooks",
              "separate clone"
            ],
            [
              "Clean tree, moving",
              "git switch"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stash Flags At A Glance"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Adds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "-u",
              "untracked files"
            ],
            [
              "-a",
              "untracked + ignored"
            ],
            [
              "-k",
              "keeps staged live"
            ],
            [
              "--staged",
              "staged only"
            ],
            [
              "-p",
              "chosen hunks"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Worked Examples & Worktree Verbs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worked Example: Hot Build"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# 10-min build, feature tree stays hot",
            "git worktree add -b fix-88 ../fix main",
            "cd ../fix && npm ci && npm test",
            "git push -u origin fix-88",
            "git worktree remove ../fix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Your feature tree keeps its warm caches",
            "No `node_modules` reinstall on the main tree",
            "Two builds run at once over one object store",
            "Nothing was stashed, so nothing can be lost"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Interrupt Without Losing Files"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash push -u -m \"wip: cart\"",
            "git switch main && git pull --rebase",
            "git switch -      # back to feature",
            "git stash pop     # then check the list"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worktree Verbs"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Verb",
            "Does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "add",
              "new checkout"
            ],
            [
              "list",
              "path, HEAD, branch"
            ],
            [
              "remove",
              "clean delete"
            ],
            [
              "prune",
              "clears stale entries"
            ],
            [
              "lock",
              "blocks prune"
            ],
            [
              "move",
              "fixes path pointers"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading Worktree List"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ git worktree list",
            "/repo        9f2c1 [main]",
            "/repo/../hf  3a71b [hotfix-501]",
            "/repo/../rev 4c0de (detached)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`(detached)` marks a throwaway checkout",
            "A row whose directory is gone stays until `prune`",
            "`--porcelain` gives a __stable__ parseable form"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Interrupt, Hotfix, Resume"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash push -u -m \"wip: cart\"",
            "git worktree add ../hf -b hotfix-501",
            "# fix, test, push from ../hf",
            "git worktree remove ../hf",
            "git stash pop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Mind the index",
          "text": "Staged work returns unstaged unless you pass `--index`, and `--index` fails outright when the index state cannot be rebuilt."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Habits That Prevent Pain"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Always label with `-m`",
            "Always include untracked with `-u`",
            "The defaults are the source of most stash pain"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Safe Scripting & Final Recall",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git config --global alias.sp \\",
            "  'stash push -u -m'",
            "git sp \"wip: checkout flow\""
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Dropped entries survive the gc window, ~30 days",
            "`git fsck --unreachable` still finds them",
            "`git stash create` prints a SHA, touches nothing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Never-Break Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Never treat `refs/stash` as storage",
            "Promote value to a branch: `git stash branch`",
            "Always remove with `git worktree remove`",
            "`prune` after any manual directory deletion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stash Anatomy Recall",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Part",
            "Holds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "tree",
              "working tree"
            ],
            [
              "parent 1",
              "HEAD at push"
            ],
            [
              "parent 2",
              "index state"
            ],
            [
              "parent 3",
              "untracked (-u)"
            ],
            [
              "stack",
              "refs/stash reflog"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Scripting Around The Stack",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "tag=\"wip-$$\"   # unique label",
            "git stash push -u -m \"$tag\"",
            "git stash list --format='%H %gs' |",
            "  grep -F \"$tag\"   # find the SHA",
            "git stash apply \"$sha\"  # not pop"
          ],
          "note": "one shared stack per repo"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==One `refs/stash`== is shared by every worktree",
            "So a bare `pop` can grab **someone else's** entry",
            "Apply by SHA, never by `stash@{n}` — indices shift"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Five commands to keep",
          "items": [
            "`git stash push -u -m msg`",
            "`git stash apply` then `drop`",
            "`git stash branch <name>`",
            "`git worktree add -b br ../dir`",
            "`git worktree list / remove / prune`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Recall line",
          "text": "Stash time-multiplexes one tree; worktrees space-multiplex many trees over one history."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Your boss pings you mid-refactor and `git switch` refuses to move. Git has two answers, and they are not interchangeable: stash is a stack of hidden 2-or-3-parent commits time-multiplexing one working tree, while worktrees space-multiplex many checkouts over one object database. 10 pages on the internals, the apply-vs-pop trap that silently duplicates your work, worktree admin rules, and a decision table for picking the right one in five seconds.",
